--- what a rollback can and cannot undo --------------------------------
  Code and frontend assets: fully reversible, update.sh --rollback.
  Database schema:          NOT reversible. The ALTERs are forward-only and
                            idempotent, so re-checking-out the old commit
                            leaves every added column in place. The
                            pre-update backup is the only way back.
  Killed jobs:              not recoverable. There is no resume.

